  "result": {
    "engine": "knitr",
    "markdown": "# Parking Regulations\n\n\n\n## General Provisions\n<ol>\n<li>All buildings and structures erected and all uses of land in all districts established after the effective date of this Ordinance shall provide accessory parking and loading facilities as required under this section.</li>\n<li>All off-street parking spaces required by this Ordinance shall be located on the same lots as the use it serves.</li>\n<li>Owners of two or more uses or parcels of land may agree to jointly utilize the same parking spaces provided that satisfactory legal evidence is presented in the form of deeds, leases, or contract documents to establish such a joint area of use.</li>\n<li>All yard area including driveways, except the required front yard for residential uses may be used for off-street parking. Garages and driveways may be considered as off-street parking spaces.</li>\n<li>A plan, drawn to scale, indicating how the off-street parking and loading requirements are to be met, shall accompany an application for a building certificate. The plan shall show all elements necessary to indicate that the requirements are being fulfilled.</li>\n<li>A parking space shall be an area ten (10) feet by eighteen (18) feet except for loading and unloading areas which shall be an area ten (10) feet by thirty-six (36) feet.</li>\n<li>If the Off-Street Parking and Off-Street Loading Requirements listed in Section 7.2 and Section 7.3 are not used, approval of the number of off-street parking spaces and locations shall be made by motion, second, and favorable vote by three-fourths of the attending Village Board members as recommended by the Planning and Zoning Commission.</li>\n<li>ADA-accessible parking space: Parking facilities for single-family, duplex, and mobile homes are exempt from the requirement. Spaces designated for the handicapped shall have minimum width of twelve feet (12) and provide a barrier free route to an accessible building entrance. Such space shall be designated with an upright sign exhibiting the universal symbol for accessibility by the handicapped. All such spaces shall be designed in compliance with the standards of the Americans with Disabilities Act.</li>\n</ol>\n\n## Off-Street Parking Requirements\nAt the time of construction, or enlargement of more than 50 percent of an existing structure or building or change in the use of land, off-street parking spaces and loading areas shall be provided, constructed, and maintained for all uses as follows:\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n\\begin{longtable}[l]{>{\\raggedright\\arraybackslash}p{15em}>{\\centering\\arraybackslash}p{15em}}\n\\toprule\n\\cellcolor{gray}{\\textcolor{white}{Use}} & \\cellcolor{gray}{\\textcolor{white}{Minimum Number of Parking Spaces}}\\\\\n\\midrule\n\\endfirsthead\n\\multicolumn{2}{@{}l}{\\textit{(continued)}}\\\\\n\\toprule\n\\cellcolor{gray}{\\textcolor{white}{Use}} & \\cellcolor{gray}{\\textcolor{white}{Minimum Number of Parking Spaces}}\\\\\n\\midrule\n\\endhead\n\n\\endfoot\n\\bottomrule\n\\endlastfoot\n\\cellcolor{gray!10}{Single family, two family dwelling} & \\cellcolor{gray!10}{2 per dwelling unit}\\\\\nApartments & \\\\\n\\cellcolor{gray!10}{Efficiency and one-bedroom} & \\cellcolor{gray!10}{1 per dwelling unit}\\\\\nTwo-bedrooms & 1.5 per dwelling unit\\\\\n\\cellcolor{gray!10}{Three or more bedrooms} & \\cellcolor{gray!10}{2 per dwelling unit}\\\\\n\\addlinespace\nMobile Trailer Park & 2 per trailer unit\\\\\n\\cellcolor{gray!10}{Hotel and Motel} & \\cellcolor{gray!10}{1 per rental unit plus 1 for every 4 employees}\\\\\nHospitals, nursing homes, rest homes, or similar uses & 1 for every 2.5 patient beds and 1 for each staff and employee on the largest shift\\\\\n\\cellcolor{gray!10}{Places of public assembly such as auditoriums, theaters, stadiums, community halls, churches, etc.} & \\cellcolor{gray!10}{1 for every 4 seats}\\\\\nBowling Alley & 2 for each alley\\\\\n\\addlinespace\n\\cellcolor{gray!10}{Retail sales department stores, restaurants, taverns, grocery stores, etc.} & \\cellcolor{gray!10}{1 per 200 square feet of floor area as determined by exterior wall dimensions}\\\\\nProfessional office establishments & 1 per 500 square feet of floor area as determined by exterior wall dimensions\\\\\n\\cellcolor{gray!10}{Manufacturing, wholesale warehouse and similar uses} & \\cellcolor{gray!10}{1 for every 2 employees on the largest working shift}\\\\*\n\\end{longtable}\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Off-Street Loading Requirements\nAt the time of construction, alteration or enlargement of any structure or building except residences and farms having an aggregate gross floor area of 500 square feet or more, off-street loading areas (areas designated adjacent to buildings where trucks may loan and unload cargo) shall be provided and maintained for all uses as follows:\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n\\begin{longtable}[l]{>{\\raggedright\\arraybackslash}p{15em}>{\\centering\\arraybackslash}p{15em}>{\\centering\\arraybackslash}p{15em}}\n\\toprule\n\\cellcolor{gray}{\\textcolor{white}{Number}} & \\cellcolor{gray}{\\textcolor{white}{Loading Area}} & \\cellcolor{gray}{\\textcolor{white}{Gross Floor Area}}\\\\\n\\midrule\n\\endfirsthead\n\\multicolumn{3}{@{}l}{\\textit{(continued)}}\\\\\n\\toprule\n\\cellcolor{gray}{\\textcolor{white}{Number}} & \\cellcolor{gray}{\\textcolor{white}{Loading Area}} & \\cellcolor{gray}{\\textcolor{white}{Gross Floor Area}}\\\\\n\\midrule\n\\endhead\n\n\\endfoot\n\\bottomrule\n\\endlastfoot\n\\cellcolor{gray!10}{One} & \\cellcolor{gray!10}{500 square feet} & \\cellcolor{gray!10}{for every 5,000 to 20,000 square feet}\\\\\nOne & 500 square feet & for every 20,000 square feet or fraction thereof\\\\*\n\\end{longtable}\n\n\n:::\n:::\n",
